@page "/team"
@attribute [Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization.Authorize(Policy = "EmployerAccount")]
<PageTitle>Team | Work-Wise</PageTitle>
<div class="page-wrap"><div class="page-title-row"><div><p class="eyebrow">FOR EMPLOYERS & PEOPLE TEAMS</p><h1>Team overview</h1><p class="page-intro">A calmer way to review leave, see upcoming absences and keep a consistent record.</p></div><span class="demo-badge">PREVIEW</span></div><div class="notice-banner"><span class="notice-symbol">i</span><div><strong>Example team only</strong><p>This screen uses fictional sample data. No employee records have been created or stored.</p></div></div>
<section class="panel"><div class="panel-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">TEAM SNAPSHOT</p><h2>At a glance</h2></div><span class="panel-icon">INFO</span></div><div class="team-stats"><div><span>Team members</span><strong>-</strong><small>Manage linked records in the employer workspace</small></div><div><span>Requests to review</span><strong>-</strong><small>Open Leave approvals for pending requests</small></div><div><span>Upcoming absences</span><strong>-</strong><small>Calendar view is not available yet</small></div></div></section><section class="panel team-empty"><div class="empty-state"><span class="empty-icon">INFO</span><h2>Your team workspace starts here</h2><p>The employer workspace supports workspace setup, employment records and private one-time employee invitation codes. Leave approvals and policy tools are available in early access. Team analytics, reports and a calendar view are not available yet.</p><a class="button-primary" href="Account/Register">Create an account <span>→</span></a></div></section><section class="security-note"><span>◇</span><p><strong>Privacy matters.</strong> Employers should only see employee information they are authorized to access. Sensitive health details are not needed to record a sick-leave absence.</p></section></div>
